  ("assistant","Your first pick is right 1 in 3 times. That never changes. So the other two doors together hold 2/3, and when the host - who knows where the car is - opens a goat door, all of that 2/3 collapses onto the single remaining door. Switching wins exactly when your first pick was wrong, which is 2/3 of the time."),
